# Generated by test/gen_reference.py — ~5.7 MB, reproducible in about a second
# from stdlib Python alone. It is deliberately NOT committed: a checked-in
# reference is a snapshot of what the core used to do, and the whole point of
# the differential is to notice when the core changes and the port does not.
# `npm test` regenerates it on every run — not only when missing — and fails if
# it cannot. A reference from before the last core change agrees with the port
# forever, which is indistinguishable from a real pass.
test/reference.json
